  "problem_statement": "feat(providers): full add/remove/update for the vision model profile\n\nVision routing (MODEL_PROFILE_VISION, executor auto-swap on image\nattachments) already worked, but the settings menu only exposed generic\nper-key editing -- no way to remove a profile, and no guided flow to stand\nup a vision profile. README claimed \"full CRUD\" that didn't actually exist.\n\n- providers.py: API_KEY_<name> now falls back to well-known providers' own\n  standard env var (OPENROUTER_API_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, ...) so an\n  already-set key works without duplicating it as API_KEY_<name>.\n- settings.py: new `wells config` actions -- `-` removes a profile (clears\n  active/cheap/vision refs that pointed to it), `v` adds/switches/clears\n  MODEL_PROFILE_VISION, suggesting a free OpenRouter vision model on create.\n- .env.example / README: document MODEL_PROFILE_VISION and the legacy-key\n  fallback.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
